    "font size" : 7.97,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "Under the conditions employed, rhesus monkeys could be reli- 454 ably acclimated to undergo fMRI scans while awake. The integrity 455 of the imaging data necessitated that subjects were minimally 456 stressed and near motionless. To objectively assess the effective- 457 ness of the training procedure in minimizing any stress to the 458 subject, physiological and endocrine measurements were taken, in 459 fully acclimated subjects, over 2h sessions in either the custom 460 fMRI apparatus or in a standard primate chair (with the exception 461 of the respiratory rate data—see Section 2). In each condition, phys- 462 iological measurements were taken over three sessions whereas 463 endocrine measurements were taken over two sessions. In the 464 custom fMRI cradle, one-way RM ANOVA reveal no main effect 465 of heart rate (F2,2 =0.295; p=0.760), respiratory rate (F2,2 =2.027; 466"
  }, {
